    "id": "liquid_knockover_fault_v1_renamed",
    "name": "Knock a beaker of hypochlorite over with another one",
    "output": "outputs/liquid_knockover",
    "limitations": [
      "Physical PBF particles stand for the beakers' liquid: each carries initial volume / seeded particles; no viscosity, wetting or surface tension calibration",
      "Particle density for rigid coupling is 10 kg/m^3, not water's: with water density the coarse particles launched the receiver beaker; particle mass is not the liquid's mass",
      "PhysX advances each 120 Hz execution step in 4 substeps of 1/480 s so fast particles cannot cross the receiver's thin wall or floor in one step; with finer substeps the fingers rest at a larger contact gap, so the bilateral grasp gap tolerance is 0.8 mm",
      "Containers are source.usdc's glass scaled to 0.6 (assets/pipetting/small_beaker.usda) resting free on pedestals by gravity; grasping uses the constraint proxy",
      "Liquid fate is a geometric inference from particle readback (sim/liquid_escape_detector.md)",
      "Fault variant: the hand carries beaker_b through beaker_a instead of pouring",
      "The push operation's force-feedback limits are raised so the sweep knocks the beaker over instead of stopping on contact",
      "Particles are seeded two spacings off the walls (closer seeding knocked a dynamic container over on the first step), so 25 mL is about 108 particles of ~231 uL each"
    ]
  },
